<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶφι</span></b>  (A) (instrum. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴς</span>, q.v.), 
			Ep.
		
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by force</i> or
			<i>might</i>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, but only with four Verbs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶ. ἀνάσσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.38
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶ. μάχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.151
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶ. δαμῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.417
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.156
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοὸς ἶ. κταμένοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.375
				</span></i>
			; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶ. βιησάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					90
				</span></i>
			, etc.—Freq. in prop. names, e.g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰφιάνασσα, Ἰφιγένεια, Ἰφιγόνη,
				Ἰφιδάμας, Ἴφικλος, ϝιφιάδας</span>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
